   "subtitles": [
    {
     "text": "Inside an app, the pointer picks the exact thing. Here's Figma. I point at the button, hold Option, and talk.",
     "out": 0.2,
     "dur": 6.21
    },
    {
     "text": "Glance doesn't guess what this means. It asks Figma to select the layer under my pointer, so I can see exactly what my words will change.",
     "out": 8.4,
     "dur": 8.09
    },
    {
     "text": "I don't wait for it. Each command becomes its own task, and they all run in parallel.",
     "out": 19.69,
     "dur": 4.95
    },
    {
     "text": "Changed my mind? Pointing at the same layer again joins the task that's already there.",
     "out": 30.54,
     "dur": 5.18
    },
    {
     "text": "Workers can call Muse Image too. It paints the picture, and Glance drops it straight into the layer.",
     "out": 51.019999999999996,
     "dur": 5.82
    },
    {
     "text": "Nothing counts as done until the reviewer checks it. It reads every change back from Figma, makes sure it matches my words, flags anything else that moved, and asks Muse Spark for a second opinion. If the check fails, the worker gets one more try.",
     "out": 62.24639198303223,
     "dur": 15.38
    },
    {
     "text": "Every task lives behind the mascot. I can pause, edit, or cancel. And undo puts the layer back exactly the way it was.",
     "out": 78.22639198303223,
     "dur": 7.94
    }
   ],
